diff --git a/docs/extensions/v1.1.md b/docs/extensions/v1.1.md
index ff2ee1f7..441c7b61 100644
--- a/docs/extensions/v1.1.md
+++ b/docs/extensions/v1.1.md
@@ -4195,3 +4195,20 @@ SDKs: Rust `Handler::resolve_debug(&DebugResolve) -> Resolved` (`Unchanged`, `Co
 `Refuse`); Go `DebugResolver.ResolveDebug` (nil to launch unchanged, `ErrDebugCancelled`, any other
 error refuses; `req.Context` ends with `0 cancel`); C the `debug_resolve` handler (0, 1 with `out`,
 -1 with `why`, -2). `rhun-ext-check` asks every `resolve = yes` debugger once per template section.
+
+## Audio output (experimental local build)
+
+`[needs] audio = yes` permits playback through the system audio output. It does not permit
+microphone capture. On macOS this grants the Core Audio output services and AudioIO shared
+memory needed by AudioQueue and Audio Units. The permission is shown at installation and on
+the extension page, and adding it during an update triggers the existing wider-access review.
+Older hosts ignore this key, so extensions must handle unavailable audio gracefully.
+
+## Paired picture keys (experimental macOS local build)
+
+`view-key-state` requires `views` and `view-keys`. In this local macOS implementation it adds
+`0 view VIEW key-up MODS NAME` paired with the existing key event, and
+`0 view VIEW mods MODS` when modifiers change. Key repeats remain ordinary key events.
+Window activation sends the focused picture `focus 1` or `focus 0`. Extensions must clear
+held keys on focus loss and closure. Bound editor commands keep their keys. Older hosts
+do not negotiate this feature; extensions may fall back to short key pulses.
